   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender equality</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-Solomon Islands partnership on Ending Violence Against Women and Girls (EVAWG) supports response services for gender-based violence victims through the SafeNet referral pathway, the Christian Care Centre (CCC) and the Family Support Centre (FSC). In partnership with the International Women&#x2019;s Development Agency (IWDA) the EVAWG program continues to provide quality legal support, counselling and case management services for victims and survivors of gender-based violence across the country. CCC is the primary provider of shelter and psychosocial support to victims and survivors of GBV in Guadalcanal. Under a partnership with IWDA, DFAT is improving and strengthening the SAFENET referral network, enabling a more responsive and coordinated survivor-centred approach.  
&#x200d;
With Australia&#x2019;s support, the two crisis centres (FSC and CCC) operate 24/7 and have assisted more than 1,244 women and girls experiencing gender-based violence. This assistance includes counselling, legal aid, case management, shelter and psychosocial support through the SAFENET referral network.</narrative>
    </description>
